- id: publication-unmoved-main
  given: An accepted Candidate while control is clean, attached to B, and B is still at A.
  when: The controller publishes.
  then: >-
    One commit with the Intent title, source changes and Complete package is created in the
    Candidate under today's size limits, `.kogen/runtime/` rejection, index-flag refusal, trailers
    and commit hooks. B is fast-forwarded to it with control's index and working tree
    synchronized, and control's HEAD, tree and clean status are asserted. Control's ignored
    Approved copy of this slug is removed. The Candidate worktree is removed without `--force`,
    the branch with `git branch -d`, and the owner record is deleted; the harness home is kept.
    `git worktree list` is back to its pre-Build entries. `build-summary.json` and `evidence.md`
    resolve the full record from control. No merge commit, rebase or re-verification happens. If
    worktree removal is refused after the fast-forward (for example the Candidate holds an
    untracked file), B stays published, the Candidate worktree, branch and owner record are kept
    with owner status `published: cleanup refused: <reason>` and the tracking record's
    disposition `published-retained`, the Build exits zero with a warning that names the path and
    `mix kogen.candidates.remove <build-id>`, and that command later removes it without
    `--discard-accepted` because the commit is reachable from B.
  wrong_result: >-
    It commits in control from Candidate bytes; updates the ref with `update-ref` and leaves
    control's index stale; force-removes a Candidate holding untracked files; leaves the branch
    behind; or deletes the harness home before the transcripts can be audited.
  verified_by: [check]
  evidence: >-
    Offline publication tests assert the commit parent is A, control status after the
    fast-forward, removal of the Approved copy, worktree, branch and owner record, the kept harness
    home, the untracked-file refusal, and fault injection before the fast-forward.
  proof:
    offline: [test/kogen/build_workspace_test.exs, test/kogen/commit_provenance_test.exs, test/kogen/commit_failure_rollback_test.exs]
    paid_target: none
    paid_reason: >-
