   718	  accepting a new pin.
   719	
   720	## Evidence ownership
   721	
   722	- `check` owns everything deterministic: topology, harness-home and credential
   723	  wiring, routing sentinels, controller verification in the Candidate,
   724	  same-Candidate rework in the fake lifecycle, Shaping during a Build,
   725	  publication and refusal, retention, records and the commands, plus the write
   726	  boundary's profile, every refusal and allowed write (real `sandbox-exec`, fake
   727	  roles), the Codex scope denials and every fail-closed and inherited case.
   728	- `live-shape-to-build` owns the Claude Code provider-only observables:
   729	  - a real Claude Code Developer logs in through the scope reference from a
   730	    per-Build config dir;
   731	  - its session resumes there in the Candidate cwd after a controller-failed
   732	    verification;
   733	  - the real Reviewer on the default route's Reviewer harness (Claude Code
   734	    while `default_route` stays `claude`; the paid fixture copies the
   735	    repository's `.kogen/config.yaml`) runs in the same Candidate. The Codex
   736	    Reviewer's Candidate cwd and per-Build operation root are proved offline
   737	    only;
   738	  - the fixture's `main` is fast-forwarded and the Candidate is removed;
   739	  - the real interactive Shape session before it still uses the scope's own
   740	    config dir with the same login;
   741	  - the real Claude Code Developer (fresh and resumed) and Reviewer run to
   742	    acceptance inside the write boundary, and a write from their process trees
   743	    into the fixture's control checkout and its Git refs is refused (scenario
   744	    `role-write-boundary`).
   745	- `live-reviewer-rework` owns the one Codex provider-only observable. Its nested
   746	  Build already runs the hybrid route every batch Build uses, and its real Codex
   747	  Reviewer returns both verdicts inside the boundary, with rollouts, login refresh
   748	  and bookkeeping in the granted Codex scope (scenario `codex-roles-inside-boundary`).
