     1	defmodule Kogen.Build do
     2	  @moduledoc """
     3	  The synchronous Build loop: preconditions, one Developer launch,
     4	  controller-owned verification after every Developer turn, a fresh Review,
     5	  bounded Rework (at most `outer_resumptions` resumes of the exact Developer
     6	  thread), and one ordinary Git Commit carrying the Intent identity.
     7	
     8	  After each Developer turn this controller (the code loaded when the Build
     9	  started, never code from the Candidate) computes the Candidate id and runs
    10	  exactly the approved `verified_by` targets itself
    11	  (`Kogen.Build.Verification`). A failed cycle resumes the exact Developer
    12	  session with the failed target's receipt and log paths, counting against
    13	  `verification_retries` and never the outer allowance; exhaustion stops the
    14	  Build before Jev and Review. No child process ever receives a verification
    15	  or tracking context.
    16	
    17	  After controller verification settles, controller code builds the handoff
    18	  report (`Kogen.Build.Report`). The Developer's final message is free prose
    19	  that no Kogen code parses: Build records it as unverified notes and asks
    20	  TypeSafe Jev (`Kogen.Jev`) once what the Developer says about each item.
    21	  Only a confident contract objection stops the Build, unless an earlier
    22	  controller cycle of the same attempt failed and its final cycle passed on
    23	  the settled Candidate: that objection is superseded and reaches the Reviewer
    24	  as an advisory item. Every other reading, and any Jev failure, reaches the
    25	  fresh Reviewer as advisory notes. Each Reviewer starts from one bounded
    26	  review packet per attempt (`Kogen.Build.ReviewPacket`).
