- id: failure-retention
  given: >-
    Builds stopped by verification exhaustion, outer-allowance exhaustion, a Jev cannot-comply
    stop, an integrity failure, a provider failure and a malformed Review.
  when: Each Build stops, and afterwards a new Build of the same Intent is started.
  then: >-
    Each stopped Build keeps its Candidate worktree, branch and harness home unchanged. The stop
    message names the slug, build id, worktree path and branch next to the tracking record path,
    plus `mix kogen.candidates.remove <build-id>`. The record's `candidate.disposition` is
    `retained` and the owner record's status is `stopped: <category>`. Control is unchanged and
    the Approved package stays in control. The new Build creates a new Candidate and harness home
    and never adopts, reuses or deletes a retained one or any foreign worktree.
  wrong_result: >-
    A stop deletes the Candidate and loses the evidence; the message omits it; or the next Build
