- id: candidate-commands
  given: >-
    Two control checkouts of different projects share one spaced `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`. Project
    P has a stopped Candidate with uncommitted edits, an accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit
    is not reachable from its admitted branch, a second accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit
    the Shaper has since fast-forwarded onto that branch, a
    `running` Candidate whose Build holds the lock, and a stale `running` record whose Build is
    gone. Project Q has a stopped Candidate. P also has a foreign worktree.
  when: >-
    From P the Shaper runs `mix kogen.candidates` and `mix kogen.candidates.remove <id>`, with and
    without `--discard-accepted`.
  then: >-
    List shows only P's Candidates with build id, slug, title, status (the stale one as
    `stopped: interrupted`), start time, branch and path. Remove deletes a stopped Candidate's
    worktree, branch, harness home and owner record; refuses the running one. For a Candidate
    holding a commit, the matrix is exact: commit reachable from the admitted branch (for example
    after the Shaper fast-forwarded it, or `published: cleanup refused`) is removed without a flag;
    commit not reachable is refused without `--discard-accepted` and removed with it. Remove
    refuses an id that is not P's, and a path that does not
    match its owner record or is not registered in P's `git worktree list`. Q's Candidate, the
    running Candidate and the foreign worktree survive. Each command prints what it removed or
    refused.
  wrong_result: >-
