- id: role-write-boundary
  given: >-
    An admitted Build with its Candidate worktree, harness home and a spaceless per-Build temp
    directory, on a route whose roles use both Claude Code and Codex. Outside the grants there are
    the control checkout (tracked files, `.kogen/`, Git metadata), a second retained Candidate and
    its harness home, the owner records, both login scopes, a symlink and a `/tmp` alias path that
    point outside, and a test-owned sentinel directory. The fake role executable
    `test/support/fake_boundary_role` tries the writes below and records each result in a receipt
    under the harness home.
  when: >-
    The controller launches the fresh Developer, a helper child and a `make` grandchild, an exact
    resume, the Reviewer and a cross-harness Expert through `mix kogen.expert`, each through the
    real adapter launch path.
  then: >-
    Every role process runs as `/usr/bin/sandbox-exec -p <profile> ...`. The profile is one
    Build-wide profile, `Kogen.Build.WriteBoundary.render/1`, built at admission from canonical
    paths. It has `(allow default)` and `(deny file-write*)`, and writes are allowed only under these
    paths: the Candidate; the harness home; the Build temp dir, which is also every launch's
    `TMPDIR`, `TMPPREFIX` and `CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR`; the stdio devices; and the named
    shared-login-state exceptions (the login keychain file and its `.sb-` temp files,
    `<Claude scope>/.oauth_refresh.lock`, and the Codex scope as scenario codex-roles-inside-boundary
    states). The controller's `KOGEN_RAW_LOG_DIR` is not granted; role launches get
    `KOGEN_RAW_LOG_DIR=<harness home>/raw-log`, which the controller copies into its own at every
    Build exit. `/bin/ps` is the only
    no-sandbox exec. `lsopen` and `appleevent-send` are denied. From inside each role, a helper,
    the `make` grandchild and a background child that outlives the role, writes into the Candidate,
    the harness home and the temp dir succeed. Each of these writes fails with EPERM and leaves
    the bytes unchanged: create, append, delete, rename, chmod, hardlink or symlink-follow into
    the control checkout (including `.kogen/` and `.kogen/build.lock`); `git commit`,
    `git update-ref` and `git config` against control's Git metadata; the controller's own
    `KOGEN_RAW_LOG_DIR` (placed inside control's `.kogen/runtime/` in the test); the other Candidate and its
    harness home; an owner record; the Claude scope's `settings.json`; the sentinel; the same
    paths through their `/tmp` aliases. A nested `sandbox-exec` with a permissive profile exits
    71. The tracking record's `boundary` block has mode `applied`, the profile's sha256 and the
    grant list. In the real fixture Build, a project SessionStart hook (in the fixture only) inside
    the real Claude Code Developer (fresh and resumed) and Reviewer process trees records
    successful writes inside the grants: the Build temp dir for every session, and the Candidate's
    ignored `.kogen/runtime/` for Developer sessions only, so the Reviewer never changes the
    Candidate. The same hook's write into an existing directory of the fixture's control checkout
    (`.kogen/runtime/boundary-escape/`) and its `git update-ref` into control's refs are refused
    with "Operation not permitted". Neither the file nor the ref exists afterwards, and the nested
    record's boundary mode is `applied`.
  wrong_result: >-
    The boundary wraps only the first Developer launch, not resumes, the Reviewer or the Expert; it
    uses non-canonical paths, so the grants silently never match; it grants `/private/tmp`, `$HOME`
    or control; it relies on Claude Code permissions or Codex's own sandbox, which don't cover the
    harness process's own writes; or Kogen asserts on the launch arguments while the real process
    is unconfined.
  verified_by: [check, live-shape-to-build]
  evidence: >-
    write_boundary_test.exs renders the profile for Claude-only, Codex-only and hybrid routes and
    asserts the exact grant list. It then runs real `sandbox-exec` launches through the Claude and
    Codex adapters with `KOGEN_HARNESS` naming `fake_boundary_role`, which runs every write, a
    `make` grandchild, a `nohup` child, a nested `sandbox-exec`, an `open -g -a` of a test app
    (LaunchServices) and an `osascript` Apple Event, and writes a JSON receipt of exit codes and
    errno values to the harness home. The receipt must show `open` and `osascript` failing. The test asserts each result, the unchanged bytes (sha256) of
    every protected path, the absence of every attempted outside file and ref, and a control launch
    where the same inside writes succeed. harness_role_test.exs covers the Expert launch from the
    Developer's tree. The paid run adds the fixture-only `.claude/settings.json` SessionStart probe
    through `KOGEN_RAW_LOG_DIR`, and live_shape_to_build_test.exs asserts the receipts per session
    id, the absent escape file and ref, and the record's boundary block.
  proof:
    offline: [test/kogen/write_boundary_test.exs, test/kogen/harness_role_test.exs, test/kogen/claude_code_harness_test.exs, rehearse-live-shape-to-build]
