   356	      linked file. Admission creates the Candidate with `git worktree add`, the `deps/` copy
   357	      and a fresh harness home and temp dir, none of which make hardlinks, and the `deps/`
   358	      copy must not use `cp -l`. Other macOS services a role could ask to write on its behalf
   359	      are not claimed to be closed (risk `service-delegation`).
   360	    - **The launcher.** `Kogen.Harness` Build role launches (adapters' `run_with_stdin`, the
   361	      Codex review and exec paths, Build readiness such as `claude auth status` and
   362	      `codex login status`) take the boundary from the launch context and prefix the command.
   363	      Readiness runs inside the boundary too, so a grant a real harness needs fails before any
   364	      model call. Shape, login, status outside a Build, and Shaping sessions are not wrapped.
   365	      Their containment is the Shaping half of BLD-12, owned by
   366	      `headless-shaping-and-question-inbox`. Every wrapped launch sets `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` to
   367	      the profile sha256. Kogen's own state root (`~/Library/Application Support/Kogen/…`:
   368	      runtimes, selectors, Codex `operations/` and `active/` leases) is outside the grants. So
   369	      `mix kogen.expert` run from the Developer's tree in a Build takes no Codex lease and makes
   370	      no operation dir there. It uses the frozen binding from `KOGEN_EXPERT`, puts its
   371	      operation root under the harness home, and relies on the lease the Build controller
   372	      already holds for that harness from admission to exit (`Harness.open_roles/3`).
   373	    - **Fails closed.** Every grant is resolved to its canonical path first, because the
   374	      kernel matches only real paths and `/tmp/…` or `/var/folders/…` aliases would silently
   375	      never match (probe 14). If `/usr/bin/sandbox-exec` is missing, a grant can't be resolved
   376	      to an existing directory, a grant is `/`, `/private/tmp`, `/private/var`, `$HOME`, the control
   377	      root or one of its ancestors, or the admission self-test (the profile applied to
   378	      `/usr/bin/true`) fails, admission stops before any readiness call or launch, naming the
   379	      reason. There is no unwrapped fallback.
   380	    - **Already confined.** The kernel refuses to apply a different profile inside a sandbox
   381	      (`sandbox_apply: Operation not permitted`, probe 2). Confinement is detected by the kernel,
   382	      never by the environment: applying `(version 1)(allow default)` to `/usr/bin/true` exits 71
   383	      only inside a sandbox. If it is not confined, `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` is ignored and the
   384	      profile is applied. If it is confined:
   385	      - `mix kogen.expert` run from a role of the admitted Build launches without re-applying,
   386	        inside that Build's own profile. Its record entry says `inherited`.
   387	      - A `mix kogen.build` whose roles use a managed harness runtime stops before admission:
   388	        "a Build cannot start inside another Build's role boundary". A real Build always gets
   389	        its own profile from an unconfined controller, so it can never run with someone
   390	        else's grants.
   391	      - A `mix kogen.build` whose roles are `KOGEN_HARNESS` test executables, meaning an offline
   392	        fixture Build a Developer runs in its shell, runs `inherited` if the marker is set. It
   393	        still can't write outside the enclosing Build's grants, but it makes no claim about
   394	        its own worktree. Its record says so. This is a restriction on the nested Build, not
   395	        an exemption from the boundary.
   396	      - Confined without the marker (a foreign sandbox): the Build stops, naming it.
   397	    - **The controller stays outside.** The parent controller and its own verification children
   398	      (#4: `make check` and the selected targets, `make -C <Candidate>`, plus proof-selector and
   399	      base-suite runs, all started by `Kogen.Build.VerificationRunner` as the controller's own
   400	      supervised children) run unconfined, with `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` removed from their
   401	      environment (added to `VerificationRunner`'s scrub list, `verification_runner.ex:17` at
   402	      9ff7af6e). The controller must write the
   403	      record, lock and receipts, and fixture Builds inside `check` and live targets must apply
   404	      their own boundary, which the kernel would refuse inside another profile.
   405	    - **Kept flags.** Claude Code keeps `--dangerously-skip-permissions`. Codex keeps
   406	      `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` and `--dangerously-bypass-hook-trust`. The
   407	      enforcement is the enclosing kernel profile, which already covers everything those
   408	      harness layers would, including the harness's own writes, and Codex's own Seatbelt would
   409	      fail to nest inside it (probe 10). README says so.
   410	    - **Record.** The tracking record gains a `boundary` block: mode (`applied` or `inherited`),
   411	      the profile sha256, the grant list, the denied scope entries and the `sandbox-exec` path.
   412	
   413	## Installing this Intent (self-hosting, D9)
   414	
   415	The installing Build runs under main's controller at `9ff7af6e` (#1, #2 and #4; #3 is parked), in
   416	the one checkout, not isolated, on `--route claude-dominant-adversarial-codex` (Claude Code
   417	Developer, Codex Reviewer and Expert), launched with every Kogen module preloaded
   418	(`mix run --no-start -e '… Code.ensure_loaded … Mix.Task.run("kogen.build", args)'`,
   419	build-failure lesson 17). It reads several files **from disk at run
   420	time**, so the Candidate must leave them byte-identical:
   421	
   422	- `.codex/hooks.json` and `.codex/hooks/**`. `VerificationPolicy.preflight`
   423	  byte-compares the PreToolUse command before every Developer launch
   424	  (`lib/kogen/verification_policy.ex:20,34-49,66-92` at `9ff7af6e`: #4's preflight requires only
   425	  `.codex/hooks/verification_policy.py` and the PreToolUse registration), and the Stop bootstrap
   490	   a helper's `git -C <control> update-ref …` or a Write-tool edit of
   491	   `~/.zshrc` fails with "Operation not permitted", while its edits in the
   492	   Candidate, its session files in the harness home and its here-documents
   493	   in the Build temp dir work. The record says `boundary: applied`.
   494	8. The controller commits in the Candidate, checks `main == A` and a clean
   495	   control, and fast-forwards `main`. Control shows the commit and a clean
   496	   status, the worktree and branch are gone, and the harness home keeps the
   497	   transcripts.
   498	
   499	Plausible implementations that pass naive checks but miss the outcome:
   500	
   501	- The worktree exists and roles `cd` there, but Candidate id, changed paths,
   502	  guards or selectors are still computed from control. Control is clean at
   503	  `A`, so the report says "no changes", and a missing selector looks present.
   504	- `make` targets still run in control (or in `File.cwd!()`), so a failing
   505	  Candidate passes against control's clean tree.
   506	- A per-Build `HOME` for Claude Code. Every role then reports "not logged in"
   507	  (probe B). Or a fresh `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` without the secure-storage
   508	  reference (probe C). Or a copied `.credentials.json` or Keychain export: a
   509	  forbidden copy that forks the refresh token.
   510	- The login scope is keyed on the Candidate path, so a project-scope login is
   511	  never found. Or the scope is re-resolved per launch, so a mid-Build selector
   512	  change switches logins inside one Build.
   513	- Inherited `CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR` is left alone, so an empty value
   514	  silently uses the personal login (probe F).
   515	- Hook commands and settings are rewritten to "run from control". That
   516	  reintroduces the `cFnHwg7P` preflight failure under main's controller and
   517	  isn't needed, because the controller already judges.
   518	- Guard capture still includes control's ignored files, so a mid-Build Draft
   519	  fails the Build.
   520	- `_build/` is copied, carrying links into control.
   521	- Publication uses `update-ref` and leaves control's index stale, or treats
   522	  "no conflicts" as publishable after `main` moved.
   523	- Removal is `--force` on success.
   524	- The harness home is deleted on publication before the live audit reads the
   525	  transcripts, or it is deleted with a foreign worktree.
   526	- Offline tests keep `File.cd!(repo, fn -> Build.run(slug) end)` and assert on
   527	  `repo`'s HEAD, which passes even if Build still works in the invoking
   528	  checkout.
   529	- The boundary wraps only the fresh Developer, or is set as harness
   530	  permission flags (Claude Code `permissions.deny`, Codex `--sandbox
   531	  workspace-write`) that leave the harness process's own writes and Kogen's
   532	  bypass flags in place.
   533	- Grants use `/tmp/...` or `/var/folders/...` aliases, so the kernel never
   534	  matches them and every role fails, or the fix is a broad `/private/tmp`,
   535	  `$HOME` or control grant.
   536	- `sandbox-exec` failing (missing, or `sandbox_apply` refused) falls back to
   537	  an unwrapped launch, or an inherited `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` alone turns the
   538	  boundary off.
   539	- The controller's `make check` runs inside a role boundary, so every
   540	  fixture Build in the suite fails with `sandbox_apply: Operation not
   541	  permitted`, or fixtures pass by special-casing `KOGEN_HARNESS`.
   542	- The Codex scope is left unwritable (the real Reviewer can't write its
   543	  rollout or refresh its login) or fully writable (a role plants
   544	  `hooks.json` or `plugins/`, lesson 3).
   545	
   546	Each scenario names the sentinel or control that rejects these.
   547	
   548	## Appetite and non-goals

