.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/audit-2026-09-25/jev-weak-clause-request.json:1:{"questions":{"weak:per-build-harness-home":{"criteria":{"c0":"Every Claude Code launch of the Build has `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` equal to `<harness home>/claude`, `CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR` equal to the scope path resolved from the control root at admission, and the caller's real `HOME`; every variable that `Kogen.ClaudeCode.environment/2` removes at 2909f557 (the `ANTHROPIC_`, `CLAUDE_CODE_`, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` and `CLAUDECODE` prefixes, `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK`, `VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE`) plus the inherited `CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR` is absent or replaced, asserted in the environment the launched child process actually sees.","c1":"Every Codex launch has `CODEX_HOME` equal to its scope, its operation root (private `HOME`, `XDG_*`, sqlite) under `<harness home>/codex`, and every variable in Codex's existing blocked set (including `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`) removed.","c2":"Readiness ran with the Build's own launch environment before any model launch.","c3":"The switched selector does not change any later launch of the running Build.","c4":"The owner record and tracking record name each binding (harness, scope name and path, runtime version).","c5":"A Claude scope directory's file list is identical before and after a fake Build, and a Codex scope differs at most by the two deterministic files Kogen already maintains there (`environments.toml`, `agents/kogen_boundary.toml`), pre-seeded in the fixture; no credential file in either scope is created, copied, linked, moved, renamed or rewritten by Kogen, no Kogen code path invokes `security` or opens a credential file, and a marker written into one Build's harness home is absent from a second Build's launch environment and home.","c6":"Every other Kogen Claude Code launch (Shape, login, status) sets `CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR` equal to its `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, overriding an inherited value.","c7":"In the real fixture, the Build's Developer transcript (with its session id from the tracking record) exists under `<harness home>/claude/projects/` and not under the scope's `projects/`, the Developer completed a turn and a resume there, the tracking record's Claude binding names the scope path, and the Shape session's transcripts are under that scope's `projects/`."},"instructions":{"rules":["Judge only observability by the named tests/targets"],"task":"For scenario per-build-harness-home (in state), which single clause of its then is LEAST directly observable by its named proof (offline selectors and paid target)?"},"type":"choice"},"weak:same-candidate-rework":{"criteria":{"c0":"In the fake lifecycle, the Developer, both resumes and both Reviewers run with cwd equal to the same single Candidate and use the same harness home; no second worktree or harness home is created; both resumes carry the first session id; each Review is a new Reviewer session; and the outer-attempt and verification-retry counters equal those two_outer_resumptions_test expects today.","c1":"In the real fixture Build (which exercises a controller-failed verification and its resume, not a Review rework), the Claude Code Developer's transcript records the Candidate path as its cwd for both the first turn and the resumed turn under one session id, the real Reviewer session records the same Candidate cwd, the fixture's main is fast-forwarded to the Intent commit, and no Candidate worktree or branch remains."},"instructions":{"rules":["Judge only observability by the named tests/targets"],"task":"For scenario same-candidate-rework (in state), which single clause of its then is LEAST directly observable by its named proof (offline selectors and paid target)?"},"type":"choice"}},"state":{"scenarios":[{"evidence":"Offline: ClaudeCode and Codex environment tests assert the exact deltas, including the inherited empty `CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR` control; fake-harness Builds record every launch's `HOME`, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, `CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR` and `CODEX_HOME`, flip the selector mid-Build, snapshot the scope directory's file list before and after, put a recording fake `security` first on PATH to assert it is never invoked by Kogen code, and run two Builds in sequence with a planted marker. Paid: live_shape_to_build_test.exs asserts the transcript locations and the binding named in `then`, using RootProfileAudit.sessions_root(fixture), which must cover both the scope and the project's harness homes.","id":"per-build-harness-home","proof":{"affected_paths":["lib/kogen/claude_code.ex","lib/kogen/codex.ex","lib/kogen/codex/environment.ex","lib/kogen/codex/state.ex","lib/kogen/harness.ex","lib/kogen/harness/claude.ex","lib/kogen/harness/codex.ex","lib/kogen/build.ex","lib/kogen/build/workspace.ex","lib/kogen/build/tracking.ex","test/kogen/harness_home_test.exs","test/kogen/claude_code_management_test.exs","test/kogen/codex_environment_test.exs","test/kogen/root_profile_audit_test.exs","test/kogen/live_shape_to_build_test.exs","test/support/root_profile_audit.ex","test/support/fake_claude","test/support/fake_codex","README.md","workflows/claude-code-runtime-upgrade.md","priv/kogen/test-reliability.yaml","priv/kogen/test-reliability-remediation.yaml"],"offline":["test/kogen/harness_home_test.exs","test/kogen/claude_code_management_test.exs","test/kogen/codex_environment_test.exs","test/kogen/root_profile_audit_test.exs"],"paid_reason":"provider-required: live-shape-to-build; observation: the managed Claude Code runtime authenticates a real Developer, and resumes its session, from a per-Build CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR through CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR pointing at the Shape session's scope, with the real Keychain; offline-limit: a fake harness cannot show that the real runtime resolves the Keychain item and refresh lock from the reference instead of the config dir","paid_target":"live-shape-to-build"},"then":"Every Claude Code launch of the Build has `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` equal to `<harness home>/claude`, `CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR` equal to the scope path resolved from the control root at admission, and the caller's real `HOME`; every variable that `Kogen.ClaudeCode.environment/2` removes at 2909f557 (the `ANTHROPIC_`, `CLAUDE_CODE_`, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` and `CLAUDECODE` prefixes, `AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK`, `VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE`) plus the inherited `CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR` is absent or replaced, asserted in the environment the launched child process actually sees. Every Codex launch has `CODEX_HOME` equal to its scope, its operation root (private `HOME`, `XDG_*`, sqlite) under `<harness home>/codex`, and every variable in Codex's existing blocked set (including `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`) removed. Readiness ran with the Build's own launch environment before any model launch. The switched selector does not change any later launch of the running Build. The owner record and tracking record name each binding (harness, scope name and path, runtime version). A Claude scope directory's file list is identical before and after a fake Build, and a Codex scope differs at most by the two deterministic files Kogen already maintains there (`environments.toml`, `agents/kogen_boundary.toml`), pre-seeded in the fixture; no credential file in either scope is created, copied, linked, moved, renamed or rewritten by Kogen, no Kogen code path invokes `security` or opens a credential file, and a marker written into one Build's harness home is absent from a second Build's launch environment and home. Every other Kogen Claude Code launch (Shape, login, status) sets `CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR` equal to its `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, overriding an inherited value. In the real fixture, the Build's Developer transcript (with its session id from the tracking record) exists under `<harness home>/claude/projects/` and not under the scope's `projects/`, the Developer completed a turn and a resume there, the tracking record's Claude binding names the scope path, and the Shape session's transcripts are under that scope's `projects/`."},{"evidence":"The fake lifecycle asserts one Candidate, one harness home and one session id across both resumptions. The live fixture's `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` path contains a space; the live test reads the Candidate path from the tracking record's `candidate` block and asserts the cwd recorded in the Developer transcript (both turns) and in the Reviewer's native session equals it, plus the single Developer session id, controller receipts bound to the Candidate id, the final fixture HEAD, and that the worktree and branch are gone.","id":"same-candidate-rework","proof":{"affected_paths":["lib/kogen/build.ex","lib/kogen/harness/**","test/kogen/two_outer_resumptions_test.exs","test/kogen/lifecycle_test.exs","test/kogen/live_shape_to_build_test.exs","test/support/root_profile_audit.ex","priv/kogen/test-reliability.yaml","priv/kogen/test-reliability-remediation.yaml"],"offline":["test/kogen/two_outer_resumptions_test.exs","test/kogen/lifecycle_test.exs","rehearse-live-shape-to-build"],"paid_reason":"provider-required: live-shape-to-build; observation: a real Claude Code Developer resumes its exact session in a Candidate worktree cwd after a controller-failed verification, the real Reviewer runs there, and publication fast-forwards the fixture main; offline-limit: fake harnesses cannot show that the managed runtimes find and resume a session from a worktree cwd with a per-Build config dir","paid_target":"live-shape-to-build"},"then":"In the fake lifecycle, the Developer, both resumes and both Reviewers run with cwd equal to the same single Candidate and use the same harness home; no second worktree or harness home is created; both resumes carry the first session id; each Review is a new Reviewer session; and the outer-attempt and verification-retry counters equal those two_outer_resumptions_test expects today. In the real fixture Build (which exercises a controller-failed verification and its resume, not a Review rework), the Claude Code Developer's transcript records the Candidate path as its cwd for both the first turn and the resumed turn under one session id, the real Reviewer session records the same Candidate cwd, the fixture's main is fast-forwarded to the Intent commit, and no Candidate worktree or branch remains."}]}}
