.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/audit-2026-09-25/sol-reaudit-prompt.md:42:   **Wrong implementation:** Set `KOGEN_PROJECT_ROOT` and task-context paths to the Candidate, but leave the actual native process cwd and some controller `File.cwd!()` reads on control; add weak selectors that assert only environment variables.  
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:3565:     "when": "`mix kogen.build <slug>` is admitted with `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` set to a directory whose path contains a space.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:3567:     "wrong_result": "Build keeps running in the invoking checkout, nests the worktree in the repository, writes under the real Kogen directory while `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` is set, copies `_build/`, reuses an existing directory or branch, fetches dependencies from the network, or deletes a foreign worktree during admission",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:3568:     "evidence": "Focused workspace tests with a real Git fixture, a spaced `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`, a real-root sentinel directory, a foreign worktree and a launch sentinel assert the paths, branch, owner record fields, base commit, deps copy, absence of `_build/`, Approved bytes, byte-identical control state, the absence of the volatile paths in the Candidate while control holds a `.kogen/build.lock`, and each refusal case with no launch.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:3588:     "w0": "Build keeps running in the invoking checkout, nests the worktree in the repository, writes under the real Kogen directory while `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` is set, copies `_build/`, reuses an existing directory or branch, fetches dependencies from the network, or deletes a foreign worktree during admission"
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:4056:     "then": "Every role launch (Claude and Codex adapters) has cwd and Git toplevel equal to the Candidate, and Codex trusts the Candidate as its project root. Candidate id, changed paths, guarded-path capture, proof-selector existence, report entries, review packet contents, citation snapshots, staging and commit are computed from the Candidate root passed explicitly: the Candidate-only selector counts as present and the control-only edit never appears. Lock, tracking record, verification context, state, history and receipts, prompts, route and config, and login-scope identity stay on the control root passed explicitly. `Harness.open`, `Harness.open_roles/3` (the route's per-role open from cross-harness-adversarial-roles), both adapters' `open`, `VerificationPolicy.preflight/2`, `VerificationPolicy.environment`, `GuardedPaths.capture`, `Git.changed_paths`, `VerificationPlan.load/build/missing_selectors` and `Build.Evidence.resolve` receive their root explicitly from Build (no `File.cwd!()` or `\".\"` default is used on any Build path), and a Build started from the third directory behaves identically. The same holds for the controller-owned verification that fortify-paid-verification landed: the environment `Build` hands `Kogen.Build.Verification.run_cycle/4` names both roots, the Candidate for `make -C` through `Kogen.Build.VerificationRunner.run_target/4`, `CatalogChange.check`, `TargetEvidence.capture` and every `TargetEvidence.verify` call, and control for the attempt's verification directory, so each receipt's, proof's and ledger diff's `log_path` or `path` is relative to control and `Verification.settle`, `Ledger.verify` and the publication re-checks read them from control; `Kogen.Git.candidate_id` and the Report's changed paths are computed from the Candidate. GuardedPaths' snapshot of `.git/config` and `.git/info/exclude` resolves through Git (`git rev-parse --git-path`), because a linked worktree's `.git` is a file, and a change to control's `.git/config` during the Build is still detected. `VerificationPolicy.environment`'s `KOGEN_PROJECT_ROOT` names the Candidate, whose hook the PreToolUse guard runs. `KOGEN_TASK_CONTEXT` `working_directory` names the Candidate. Every control-side locator handed to a role (the task context's `tracking_path`, the Reviewer's review-packet path in the task context and the notes section, and the verification-failure prompt's retained receipt and log) is an absolute control path that opens from the Candidate cwd, while the recorded bindings keep the control-relative forms below. Ordinary citations are Candidate-relative; the tracking-record citation and `build-summary.json` `full_record.path` resolve from control. Review packets stay at control's `.kogen/runtime/scenario-tracking/<build-id>/review-packets/<n>.json`, and the record's packet `path` and record-version `sidecar` locators stay relative to control (today `ReviewPacket` and `Tracking` compute them from `File.cwd!()`; they take the control root explicitly), because the unedited Reviewer-rework support (`Kogen.ReviewPacketAudit.audit!/4`) asserts that exact layout.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:4080:     "c7": "`VerificationPolicy.environment`'s `KOGEN_PROJECT_ROOT` names the Candidate, whose hook the PreToolUse guard runs.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:5399:     "evidence": "The fake lifecycle's per-launch receipts (written by the fake harness from inside each launched process: `pwd -P`, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, session id) assert one Candidate, one harness home and one Developer session id across both resumptions and a distinct Reviewer session per Review, and the worktree list shows a single Candidate throughout. The live fixture's `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` path contains a space; the live test reads the Candidate path from the tracking record's `candidate` block and asserts the cwd recorded in the Developer transcript (both turns) and in the Reviewer's native session equals it, plus the single Developer session id, controller receipts bound to the Candidate id, the final fixture HEAD, and that the worktree and branch are gone.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:5798:     "given": "Two control checkouts of different projects share one spaced `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`. Project P has a stopped Candidate with uncommitted edits, an accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit is not reachable from its admitted branch, a second accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit the Shaper has since fast-forwarded onto that branch, a `running` Candidate whose Build holds the lock, and a stale `running` record whose Build is gone. Project Q has a stopped Candidate. P also has a foreign worktree.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:6197:    "evidence": "Focused workspace tests with a real Git fixture, a spaced `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`, a real-root sentinel directory, a foreign worktree and a launch sentinel assert the paths, branch, owner record fields, base commit, deps copy, absence of `_build/`, Approved bytes, byte-identical control state, the absence of the volatile paths in the Candidate while control holds a `.kogen/build.lock`, and each refusal case with no launch.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:6203:     "e0": "Focused workspace tests with a real Git fixture, a spaced `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`, a real-root sentinel directory, a foreign worktree and a launch sentinel assert the paths, branch, owner record fields, base commit, deps copy, absence of `_build/`, Approved bytes, byte-identical control state, the absence of the volatile paths in the Candidate while control holds a `.kogen/build.lock`, and each refusal case with no launch."
