(`git rev-parse --git-path`), because a linked worktree's `.git` is a file, and a change to control's `.git/config` during the Build is still detected. `VerificationPolicy.environment`'s `KOGEN_PROJECT_ROOT` names the Candidate, whose hook the PreToolUse guard runs. `KOGEN_TASK_CONTEXT` `working_directory` names the Candidate. Every control-side locator handed to a role (the task context's `tracking_path`, the Reviewer's review-packet path in the task context and the notes section, and the verification-failure prompt's retained receipt and log) is an absolute control path that opens from the Candidate cwd, while the recorded bindings keep the control-relative forms below. Ordinary citations are Candidate-relative; the tracking-record citation and `build-summary.json` `full_record.path` resolve from control. Review packets stay at control's `.kogen/runtime/scenario-tracking/<build-id>/review-packets/<n>.json`, and the record's packet `path` and record-version `sidecar` locators stay relative to control (today `ReviewPacket` and `Tracking` compute them from `File.cwd!()`; they take the control root explicitly), because the unedited Reviewer-rework support (`Kogen.ReviewPacketAudit.audit!/4`) asserts that exact layout.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:11781:     "evidence": "write_boundary_test.exs runs the fake Codex role against a disposable scope-shaped directory and asserts each denied entry, the allowed writes and the retained flags. harness_role_test.exs runs `mix kogen.expert` inside a real outer profile against a fake managed Codex runtime under a disposable `KOGEN_CODEX_ROOT` (the managed open path, since `KOGEN_HARNESS` skips leases), and asserts that the Expert launch succeeds and the `active/` and `operations/` entries there are unchanged; codex_environment_test.exs asserts the Build temp `TMPDIR` and flags on Codex launches. The paid live-reviewer-rework run asserts, in `test/support/live_reviewer_rework_fixture.ex`, the retained nested record's boundary block, one SessionStart receipt per Codex Reviewer session id (from the retained raw-log copy) with the refused outside attempts, the absent escape file and ref, and the denied names against a pre-Build snapshot of the scope's top-level entries. Probe 20 showed real Codex 0.156.1 runs a project SessionStart hook on `exec` and `exec resume` inside the profile.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:12584:     "given": "Build admissions where `/usr/bin/sandbox-exec` is replaced by a missing path; where `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` is given through the `/tmp` alias of a `/private/tmp` directory; where a grant can't be resolved to an existing directory; where the rendered grants would include `/`, `/private/tmp`, `/private/var`, `$HOME`, the control root or an ancestor of it; and where the admission self-test of the profile fails. There are also a controller that already runs inside a Kogen boundary (with `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` set by it), one inside a foreign sandbox (no marker), and an unconfined controller with a spoofed `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY`.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:12588:     "evidence": "write_boundary_test.exs covers each refusal with a launch sentinel that must stay absent, plus a Build whose workspaces root is given through the `/tmp` alias: its rendered profile must contain only canonical paths and its fake role's inside write must succeed (a grant the kernel never matches would make it fail), starts one fake-harness fixture Build from inside a real outer `sandbox-exec` (with and without the marker, asserting `inherited` and a refused write outside the enclosing grants), and a managed-runtime Build (a fake runtime executable under a disposable `KOGEN_CLAUDE_ROOT`) from inside it, asserting the refusal. It also spoofs the marker in an unconfined run and asserts the raw-log copy on success and on a stop. candidate_verification_test.exs asserts that the environment of the controller's verification child lacks `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` and that a fixture Build started by that child records `applied`.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:13745:    "evidence": "write_boundary_test.exs runs the fake Codex role against a disposable scope-shaped directory and asserts each denied entry, the allowed writes and the retained flags. harness_role_test.exs runs `mix kogen.expert` inside a real outer profile against a fake managed Codex runtime under a disposable `KOGEN_CODEX_ROOT` (the managed open path, since `KOGEN_HARNESS` skips leases), and asserts that the Expert launch succeeds and the `active/` and `operations/` entries there are unchanged; codex_environment_test.exs asserts the Build temp `TMPDIR` and flags on Codex launches. The paid live-reviewer-rework run asserts, in `test/support/live_reviewer_rework_fixture.ex`, the retained nested record's boundary block, one SessionStart receipt per Codex Reviewer session id (from the retained raw-log copy) with the refused outside attempts, the absent escape file and ref, and the denied names against a pre-Build snapshot of the scope's top-level entries. Probe 20 showed real Codex 0.156.1 runs a project SessionStart hook on `exec` and `exec resume` inside the profile.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:13754:     "e1": "harness_role_test.exs runs `mix kogen.expert` inside a real outer profile against a fake managed Codex runtime under a disposable `KOGEN_CODEX_ROOT` (the managed open path, since `KOGEN_HARNESS` skips leases), and asserts that the Expert launch succeeds and the `active/` and `operations/` entries there are unchanged",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:14028:    "evidence": "write_boundary_test.exs covers each refusal with a launch sentinel that must stay absent, plus a Build whose workspaces root is given through the `/tmp` alias: its rendered profile must contain only canonical paths and its fake role's inside write must succeed (a grant the kernel never matches would make it fail), starts one fake-harness fixture Build from inside a real outer `sandbox-exec` (with and without the marker, asserting `inherited` and a refused write outside the enclosing grants), and a managed-runtime Build (a fake runtime executable under a disposable `KOGEN_CLAUDE_ROOT`) from inside it, asserting the refusal. It also spoofs the marker in an unconfined run and asserts the raw-log copy on success and on a stop. candidate_verification_test.exs asserts that the environment of the controller's verification child lacks `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` and that a fixture Build started by that child records `applied`.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:14034:     "e0": "write_boundary_test.exs covers each refusal with a launch sentinel that must stay absent, plus a Build whose workspaces root is given through the `/tmp` alias: its rendered profile must contain only canonical paths and its fake role's inside write must succeed (a grant the kernel never matches would make it fail), starts one fake-harness fixture Build from inside a real outer `sandbox-exec` (with and without the marker, asserting `inherited` and a refused write outside the enclosing grants), and a managed-runtime Build (a fake runtime executable under a disposable `KOGEN_CLAUDE_ROOT`) from inside it, asserting the refusal",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:14440:     "o0": "**Admission creates the Candidate.** From the clean, attached control checkout at commit `A` on branch `B`, Build creates one linked worktree in Kogen's own directory, outside the repository: `<workspaces-root>/<project-id>/<slug>-<build-id>/`, on a new branch `kogen/<slug>/<build-id>` at `A`. - `<workspaces-root>` is `~/Library/Application Support/Kogen/build-workspaces`, or `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` if set. Tests always set it. - `<project-id>` is the SHA-256 of the expanded control path, the same id the login selectors use (`Kogen.ClaudeCode.project_id/1`). - `<build-id>` is the scenario-tracking record id. An existing path, branch or owner record with that name is refused, never reused. Before the worktree, Kogen writes an owner record at `<workspaces-root>/<project-id>/candidates/<build-id>.json` with these fields: schema version, build id, Intent id, slug, title, control root, worktree path, branch, admitted branch and commit, harness home, credential bindings, start time, status (`running`, `stopped: <category>`, `accepted-unpublished: <reason>`) and, when one exists, the Candidate commit. The status is updated at every exit. A `running` status counts only while this project's build lock is held by a live process. Otherwise it's reported as `stopped: interrupted`. The Candidate gets a plain recursive copy of control `deps/`. If `deps/` is missing, admission stops before any launch and names `mix deps.get`; there is no network fallback. It gets no `_build/` and compiles cold. The controller's frozen Approved package bytes go to the Candidate's ignored `.kogen/intents/approved/<slug>/`. Nothing else from control's ignored state is copied: no `.kogen/build.lock`, `.kogen/runtime/`, `.kogen/codex/` or `.codex/sessions/` (build-failure lesson 13). Creation is one function in one module (`Kogen.Build.Workspace.create/\u2026`), so a later seeding step lands in one place.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:15234:    "given": "Two control checkouts of different projects share one spaced `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`. Project P has a stopped Candidate with uncommitted edits, an accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit is not reachable from its admitted branch, a second accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit the Shaper has since fast-forwarded onto that branch, a `running` Candidate whose Build holds the lock, and a stale `running` record whose Build is gone. Project Q has a stopped Candidate. P also has a foreign worktree.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:15466:    "evidence": "write_boundary_test.exs runs the fake Codex role against a disposable scope-shaped directory and asserts each denied entry, the allowed writes and the retained flags. harness_role_test.exs runs `mix kogen.expert` inside a real outer profile against a fake managed Codex runtime under a disposable `KOGEN_CODEX_ROOT` (the managed open path, since `KOGEN_HARNESS` skips leases), and asserts that the Expert launch succeeds and the `active/` and `operations/` entries there are unchanged; codex_environment_test.exs asserts the Build temp `TMPDIR` and flags on Codex launches. The paid live-reviewer-rework run asserts, in `test/support/live_reviewer_rework_fixture.ex`, the retained nested record's boundary block, one SessionStart receipt per Codex Reviewer session id (from the retained raw-log copy) with the refused outside attempts, the absent escape file and ref, and the denied names against a pre-Build snapshot of the scope's top-level entries. Probe 20 showed real Codex 0.156.1 runs a project SessionStart hook on `exec` and `exec resume` inside the profile.",
