.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:16704:    "scenario_then": "Every role launch (Claude and Codex adapters) has cwd and Git toplevel equal to the Candidate, and Codex trusts the Candidate as its project root. Candidate id, changed paths, guarded-path capture, proof-selector existence, report entries, review packet contents, citation snapshots, staging and commit are computed from the Candidate root passed explicitly: the Candidate-only selector counts as present and the control-only edit never appears. Lock, tracking record, verification context, state, history and receipts, prompts, route and config, and login-scope identity stay on the control root passed explicitly. `Harness.open`, `Harness.open_roles/3` (the route's per-role open from cross-harness-adversarial-roles), both adapters' `open`, `VerificationPolicy.preflight/2`, `VerificationPolicy.environment`, `GuardedPaths.capture`, `Git.changed_paths`, `VerificationPlan.load/build/missing_selectors` and `Build.Evidence.resolve` receive their root explicitly from Build (no `File.cwd!()` or `\".\"` default is used on any Build path), and a Build started from the third directory behaves identically. The same holds for the controller-owned verification that fortify-paid-verification landed: the environment `Build` hands `Kogen.Build.Verification.run_cycle/4` names both roots, the Candidate for `make -C` through `Kogen.Build.VerificationRunner.run_target/4`, `CatalogChange.check`, `TargetEvidence.capture` and every `TargetEvidence.verify` call, and control for the attempt's verification directory, so each receipt's, proof's and ledger diff's `log_path` or `path` is relative to control and `Verification.settle`, `Ledger.verify` and the publication re-checks read them from control; `Kogen.Git.candidate_id` and the Report's changed paths are computed from the Candidate. GuardedPaths' snapshot of `.git/config` and `.git/info/exclude` resolves through Git (`git rev-parse --git-path`), because a linked worktree's `.git` is a file, and a change to control's `.git/config` during the Build is still detected. `VerificationPolicy.environment`'s `KOGEN_PROJECT_ROOT` names the Candidate, whose hook the PreToolUse guard runs. `KOGEN_TASK_CONTEXT` `working_directory` names the Candidate. Every control-side locator handed to a role (the task context's `tracking_path`, the Reviewer's review-packet path in the task context and the notes section, and the verification-failure prompt's retained receipt and log) is an absolute control path that opens from the Candidate cwd, while the recorded bindings keep the control-relative forms below. Ordinary citations are Candidate-relative; the tracking-record citation and `build-summary.json` `full_record.path` resolve from control. Review packets stay at control's `.kogen/runtime/scenario-tracking/<build-id>/review-packets/<n>.json`, and the record's packet `path` and record-version `sidecar` locators stay relative to control (today `ReviewPacket` and `Tracking` compute them from `File.cwd!()`; they take the control root explicitly), because the unedited Reviewer-rework support (`Kogen.ReviewPacketAudit.audit!/4`) asserts that exact layout.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:17304:    "evidence": "write_boundary_test.exs covers each refusal with a launch sentinel that must stay absent, plus a Build whose workspaces root is given through the `/tmp` alias: its rendered profile must contain only canonical paths and its fake role's inside write must succeed (a grant the kernel never matches would make it fail), starts one fake-harness fixture Build from inside a real outer `sandbox-exec` (with and without the marker, asserting `inherited` and a refused write outside the enclosing grants), and a managed-runtime Build (a fake runtime executable under a disposable `KOGEN_CLAUDE_ROOT`) from inside it, asserting the refusal. It also spoofs the marker in an unconfined run and asserts the raw-log copy on success and on a stop. candidate_verification_test.exs asserts that the environment of the controller's verification child lacks `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` and that a fixture Build started by that child records `applied`.",
