.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:22000:    "entry": "5. **Shaping-preflight-audit.** Not assumed. It is parked (`plan/staging/shaping-preflight-audit-PARKED.md`). If it lands later, its Shaping-only auditor launch must go through `Kogen.ClaudeCode.environment/2`, which this Intent already makes strip and set `CLAUDE_SECURESTORAGE_CONFIG_DIR`. That is #3's concern, not this Intent's. ## The 2026-09-24 questions (history) The questions file as it stood before the 2026-09-24 reshape is kept at `historical/2026-09-22-warm-seed-revision/questions.md`. Its settled boundaries still hold and are summarized under \"Carried forward\". ## Open for the Shaper (2026-09-24, B1 reshape) The Draft currently assumes the recommended answer to each question. ### Q1. Where Candidate worktrees live \u2014 settled 2026-09-24 Shaper: \"inside Kogen's own tree\". CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md nesting is unimportant because those files are not wanted in projects; duplicate trees in the repository are the cost to avoid. The location is `~/Library/Application Support/Kogen/build-workspaces/<project-id>/`. Tests redirect the root with `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`, like `KOGEN_CLAUDE_ROOT`, so automated tests never write to the real Kogen directory; the Shaper asked what this meant and was answered. ### Q2. Kept Candidates: stop message and commands \u2014 settled 2026-09-24 The Shaper's answers across three rounds: - A Kogen command for kept Candidates is wanted, not bare git commands. - A list command is required: \"git worktree list is useless - it doesn't show which worktree belongs to which intent and the worktree names are obfuscated\". Names must be readable and list must show the Intent. - Publish is dropped: \"publish is weird because it's pretty much useless\". An accepted Build already fast-forwards automatically. - Remove is added. Guard accepted only: deleting a stopped Candidate's uncommitted edits is fine on request, but a Candidate holding an accepted commit not reachable from its admitted branch needs `--discard-accepted`. - Prune is added. Removing orphans left by deleted or moved checkouts, the only cross-project action, needs an explicit flag, \"because it's an unexpected behavior\". - Every command acts on the current project only. Narrowed after independent review (2026-09-24): the Shaper forwarded a review recommending cutting `prune` and `--orphans` to make B1 more likely to land first time, and said \"the agent was right / these other commands are unnecessary for now / we can either add those as part of parallel builds or even as a separate intent\". B1 keeps `mix kogen.candidates` (list) and `mix kogen.candidates.remove <build-id> [--discard-accepted]`. Prune, orphan cleanup and the `project.json` they needed are parked in `.kogen/runtime/shaping-followups/SHAPE_CANDIDATE_PRUNE.md`. They are not approved backlog. The command names were not vetoed. The same review's item 3 was also accepted (\"the agent was right\"): both live fixtures' `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` paths contain a space. ### Q3. The Codex route's hook configuration \u2014 settled 202"
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/repreflight-2026-09-26-9ff7af6e/jev/jev-audit.json:22110:    "given": "Build admissions where `/usr/bin/sandbox-exec` is replaced by a missing path; where `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` is given through the `/tmp` alias of a `/private/tmp` directory; where a grant can't be resolved to an existing directory; where the rendered grants would include `/`, `/private/tmp`, `/private/var`, `$HOME`, the control root or an ancestor of it; and where the admission self-test of the profile fails. There are also a controller that already runs inside a Kogen boundary (with `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` set by it), one inside a foreign sandbox (no marker), and an unconfined controller with a spoofed `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY`.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/audit-2026-09-25/sol-high-audit.md:37:   **Wrong implementation:** Set `KOGEN_PROJECT_ROOT` and task-context paths to the Candidate, but leave the actual native process cwd and some controller `File.cwd!()` reads on control; add weak selectors that assert only environment variables.  
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/failed-attempts-lessons-2026-09-25.md:28:   and `priv/kogen/claude_code/settings.json` to use `KOGEN_PROJECT_ROOT`.
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/audit-2026-09-25-write-boundary/jev-audit.json:46:     "given": "Two control checkouts of different projects share one spaced `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`. Project P has a stopped Candidate with uncommitted edits, an accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit is not reachable from its admitted branch, a second accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit the Shaper has since fast-forwarded onto that branch, a `running` Candidate whose Build holds the lock, and a stale `running` record whose Build is gone. Project Q has a stopped Candidate. P also has a foreign worktree.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/audit-2026-09-25-write-boundary/jev-audit.json:450:     "evidence": "The fake lifecycle's per-launch receipts (written by the fake harness from inside each launched process: `pwd -P`, `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`, session id) assert one Candidate, one harness home and one Developer session id across both resumptions and a distinct Reviewer session per Review, and the worktree list shows a single Candidate throughout. The live fixture's `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` path contains a space; the live test reads the Candidate path from the tracking record's `candidate` block and asserts the cwd recorded in the Developer transcript (both turns) and in the Reviewer's native session equals it, plus the single Developer session id, controller receipts bound to the Candidate id, the final fixture HEAD, and that the worktree and branch are gone.",
