.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/audit-2026-09-25-write-boundary/jev-after-sol/jev-audit.json:11440:     "given": "Build admissions where `/usr/bin/sandbox-exec` is replaced by a missing path; where `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT` is given through the `/tmp` alias of a `/private/tmp` directory; where a grant can't be resolved to an existing directory; where the rendered grants would include `/`, `/private/tmp`, `/private/var`, `$HOME`, the control root or an ancestor of it; and where the admission self-test of the profile fails. There are also a controller that already runs inside a Kogen boundary (with `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` set by it), one inside a foreign sandbox (no marker), and an unconfined controller with a spoofed `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY`.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/audit-2026-09-25-write-boundary/jev-after-sol/jev-audit.json:11444:     "evidence": "write_boundary_test.exs covers each refusal with a launch sentinel that must stay absent, plus a Build whose workspaces root is given through the `/tmp` alias: its rendered profile must contain only canonical paths and its fake role's inside write must succeed (a grant the kernel never matches would make it fail), starts one fake-harness fixture Build from inside a real outer `sandbox-exec` (with and without the marker, asserting `inherited` and a refused write outside the enclosing grants), and a managed-runtime Build (a fake runtime executable under a disposable `KOGEN_CLAUDE_ROOT`) from inside it, asserting the refusal. It also spoofs the marker in an unconfined run and asserts the raw-log copy on success and on a stop. candidate_verification_test.exs asserts that the environment of the controller's verification child lacks `KOGEN_WRITE_BOUNDARY` and that a fixture Build started by that child records `applied`.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/audit-2026-09-25-write-boundary/jev-after-sol/jev-audit.json:12235:     "evidence": "write_boundary_test.exs runs the fake Codex role against a disposable scope-shaped directory and asserts each denied entry, the allowed writes and the retained flags. harness_role_test.exs runs `mix kogen.expert` inside a real outer profile against a fake managed Codex runtime under a disposable `KOGEN_CODEX_ROOT` (the managed open path, since `KOGEN_HARNESS` skips leases), and asserts that the Expert launch succeeds and the `active/` and `operations/` entries there are unchanged; codex_environment_test.exs asserts the Build temp `TMPDIR` and flags on Codex launches. The paid live-reviewer-rework run asserts, in `test/support/live_reviewer_rework_fixture.ex`, the retained nested record's boundary block, one SessionStart receipt per Codex Reviewer session id (from the retained raw-log copy) with the refused outside attempts, the absent escape file and ref, and the denied names against a pre-Build snapshot of the scope's top-level entries. Probe 20 showed real Codex 0.156.1 runs a project SessionStart hook on `exec` and `exec resume` inside the profile.",
.kogen/intents/drafts/isolated-candidate-workspace/evidence/audit-2026-09-25-write-boundary/jev-after-sol/jev-audit.json:13468:    "given": "Two control checkouts of different projects share one spaced `KOGEN_WORKSPACES_ROOT`. Project P has a stopped Candidate with uncommitted edits, an accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit is not reachable from its admitted branch, a second accepted-unpublished Candidate whose commit the Shaper has since fast-forwarded onto that branch, a `running` Candidate whose Build holds the lock, and a stale `running` record whose Build is gone. Project Q has a stopped Candidate. P also has a foreign worktree.",
